{"type":"message","id":"09e5a1c2","parentId":"227d4a66","timestamp":"2026-03-04T04:19:48.718Z","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"text","text":"[Wed 2026-03-04 12:19 GMT+8] [Subagent Context] You are running as a subagent (depth 2/2). Results auto-announce to your requester; do not busy-poll for status.\n\n[Subagent Task]: ## Task: Add destroy() method to PixelEditor\n\n## Workspace: /home/one/projects/PixelArtEditor\n\n## Context\nH1 fix was not completed. Need to add destroy() method to prevent memory leaks.\n\n## Requirement\n**File:** `src/editor/PixelEditor.ts`\n\nAdd a `destroy()` method to clean up event listeners:\n\n```typescript\n/**\n * Clean up event listeners and resources\n * Call this when the editor is no longer needed\n */\ndestroy(): void {\n  this.#el.removeEventListener(\"pointerdown\", this);\n  this.#el.removeEventListener(\"pointermove\", this);\n  this.#el.removeEventListener(\"pointerup\", this);\n  this.#el.removeEventListener(\"pointerleave\", this);\n  this.#listeners = [];\n}\n```\n\nNote: The constructor also listens to \"pointerleave\" event, so include that too.\n\n## Deliverable\n- Add destroy() method after the clear() method\n- Verify it compiles: `npx tsc --noEmit`\n- Run tests: `npm test`\n\n## Report To: $HOME/.openclaw-reports/code-agent/"}],"timestamp":1772597988715}}
{"type":"message","id":"146748e3","parentId":"09e5a1c2","timestamp":"2026-03-04T04:19:56.470Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"I need to add a `destroy()` method to the PixelEditor class in `/home/one/projects/PixelArtEditor/src/editor/PixelEditor.ts`. Let me:\n\n1. Read the file to understand its current structure\n2. Find where to add the destroy() method (after clear() method)\n3. Add the destroy() method\n4. Verify it compiles\n5. Run tests\n6. Write a development report\n\nLet me start by reading the file.","thinkingSignature":"reasoning_content"},{"type":"text","text":"I'll add the `destroy()` method to PixelEditor.ts. Let me first read the file to understand its structure."},{"type":"toolCall","id":"tool-e99f1bc4b43f4ddeb125cc182eede274","name":"read","arguments":{"file_path":"/home/one/projects/PixelArtEditor/src/editor/PixelEditor.ts"}}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"bailian","model":"glm-5","usage":{"input":3466,"output":241,"cacheRead":8798,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":12505,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1772597988717}}
{"type":"message","id":"b0fc0151","parentId":"146748e3","timestamp":"2026-03-04T04:19:56.476Z","message":{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"tool-e99f1bc4b43f4ddeb125cc182eede274","toolName":"read","content":[{"type":"text","text":"import type { RGB, PixelDataState, ArtboardSize } from \"../types.js\";\nimport { PixelData } from \"../crdt/PixelData.js\";\nimport { Encoder } from \"../encoding/Encoder.js\";\nimport { Decoder } from \"../encoding/Decoder.js\";\n\n/**\n * Compression mode\n */\nexport type CompressionMode = \"none\" | \"binary\";\n\n/**\n * Tool mode\n */\nexport type ToolMode = \"pencil\" | \"eraser\";\n\n/**\n * PixelEditor options\n */\nexport interface PixelEditorOptions {\n  /** Enable grid overlay */\n  showGrid?: boolean;\n  /** Grid canvas element */\n  gridCanvas?: HTMLCanvasElement | null;\n  /** Overlay canvas for cursor coordinates */\n  overlayCanvas?: HTMLCanvasElement | null;\n}\n\n/**\n * PixelEditor - Canvas-based pixel art editor with CRDT sync\n */\nexport class PixelEditor {\n  /** The underlying canvas element */\n  #el: HTMLCanvasElement;\n\n  /** 2D canvas rendering context */\n  #ctx: CanvasRenderingContext2D;\n\n  /** Artboard size in drawable pixels */\n  #artboard: ArtboardSize;\n\n  /** Underlying pixel data CRDT */\n  #data: PixelData;\n\n  /** Selected drawing color */\n  #color: RGB = [0, 0, 0];\n\n  /** Previous cursor position for line drawing */\n  #prev: [x: number, y: number] | undefined;\n\n  /** Painted pixels during current drag (for timestamp optimization) */\n  #painted = new Set<string>();\n\n  /** Change event listeners */\n  #listeners: Array<(data: PixelDataState | Uint8Array) => void> = [];\n\n  /** Compression mode */\n  #compressionMode: CompressionMode = \"none\";\n\n  /** Encoder instance */\n  #encoder?: Encoder;\n\n  /** Decoder instance */\n  #decoder?: Decoder;\n\n  /** Current tool mode */\n  #toolMode: ToolMode = \"pencil\";\n\n  /** Brush size (1, 2, or 4 pixels) */\n  #brushSize: 1 | 2 | 4 = 1;\n\n  /** Grid canvas element */\n  #gridCanvas: HTMLCanvasElement | null = null;\n\n  /** Grid context */\n  #gridCtx: CanvasRenderingContext2D | null = null;\n\n  /** Show grid flag */\n  #showGrid: boolean = false;\n\n  /** Overlay canvas for cursor display */\n  #overlayCanvas: HTMLCanvasElement | null = null;\n\n  /** Overlay context */\n  #overlayCtx: CanvasRenderingContext2D | null = null;\n\n  /** Coordinate display callback */\n  #onCoordChange?: (x: number | null, y: number | null) => void;\n\n  /** Fill rate display callback */\n  #onFillRateChange?: (rate: number) => void;\n\n  /** Compression status callback */\n  #onCompressionStatus?: (status: string) => void;\n\n  /**\n   * Set the compression mode\n   */\n  set compressionMode(mode: CompressionMode) {\n    this.#compressionMode = mode;\n    if (mode === \"binary\") {\n      this.#encoder = new Encoder(this.#artboard.w, this.#artboard.h);\n      this.#decoder = new Decoder();\n    }\n  }\n\n  /**\n   * Get the compression mode\n   */\n  get compressionMode(): CompressionMode {\n    return this.#compressionMode;\n  }\n\n  /**\n   * Set the drawing color\n   */\n  set color(color: RGB) {\n    this.#color = color;\n  }\n\n  /**\n   * Get the drawing color\n   */\n  get color(): RGB {\n    return this.#color;\n  }\n\n  /**\n   * Set the tool mode (pencil or eraser)\n   */\n  set toolMode(mode: ToolMode) {\n    this.#toolMode = mode;\n    this.#updateCursor();\n  }\n\n  /**\n   * Get the tool mode\n   */\n  get toolMode(): ToolMode {\n    return this.#toolMode;\n  }\n\n  /**\n   * Set the brush size\n   */\n  set brushSize(size: 1 | 2 | 4) {\n    this.#brushSize = size;\n  }\n\n  /**\n   * Get the brush size\n   */\n  get brushSize(): 1 | 2 | 4 {\n    return this.#brushSize;\n  }\n\n  /**\n   * Set whether to show the grid\n   */\n  set showGrid(show: boolean) {\n    this.#showGrid = show;\n    this.#updateGridVisibility();\n  }\n\n  /**\n   * Get whether to show the grid\n   */\n  get showGrid(): boolean {\n    return this.#showGrid;\n  }\n\n  /**\n   * Set callback for coordinate changes\n   */\n  set onCoordChange(cb: (x: number | null, y: number | null) => void) {\n    this.#onCoordChange = cb;\n  }\n\n  /**\n   * Set callback for fill rate changes\n   */\n  set onFillRateChange(cb: (rate: number) => void) {\n    this.#onFillRateChange = cb;\n  }\n\n  /**\n   * Set callback for compression status changes\n   */\n  set onCompressionStatus(cb: (status: string) => void) {\n    this.#onCompressionStatus = cb;\n  }\n\n  /**\n   * Create a new PixelEditor\n   * @param el - Canvas element\n   * @param artboard - Artboard dimensions\n   * @param id - Unique peer ID (optional, generates UUID if not provided)\n   * @param options - Optional configuration\n   */\n  constructor(\n    el: HTMLCanvasElement,\n    artboard: ArtboardSize,\n    id?: string,\n    options?: PixelEditorOptions\n  ) {\n    this.#el = el;\n    this.#artboard = artboard;\n\n    const ctx = el.getContext(\"2d\");\n    if (!ctx) throw new Error(\"Couldn't get 2D rendering context\");\n    this.#ctx = ctx;\n\n    this.#data = new PixelData(id ?? crypto.randomUUID());\n\n    // Initialize grid canvas if provided\n    if (options?.gridCanvas) {\n      this.#gridCanvas = options.gridCanvas;\n      const gridCtx = options.gridCanvas.getContext(\"2d\");\n      if (gridCtx) {\n        this.#gridCtx = gridCtx;\n        this.#initGrid();\n      }\n    }\n\n    // Initialize overlay canvas if provided\n    if (options?.overlayCanvas) {\n      this.#overlayCanvas = options.overlayCanvas;\n      const overlayCtx = options.overlayCanvas.getContext(\"2d\");\n      if (overlayCtx) {\n        this.#overlayCtx = overlayCtx;\n      }\n    }\n\n    // Listen for pointer events\n    this.#el.addEventListener(\"pointerdown\", this);\n    this.#el.addEventListener(\"pointermove\", this);\n    this.#el.addEventListener(\"pointerup\", this);\n    this.#el.addEventListener(\"pointerleave\", this);\n\n    // Handle high-DPI displays\n    this.#el.width = this.#el.clientWidth * devicePixelRatio;\n    this.#el.height = this.#el.clientHeight * devicePixelRatio;\n    this.#ctx.scale(devicePixelRatio, devicePixelRatio);\n    this.#ctx.imageSmoothingEnabled = false;\n\n    // Initialize cursor style\n    this.#updateCursor();\n\n    // Initial draw\n    this.#draw();\n  }\n\n  /**\n   * Add a change listener\n   */\n  set onchange(listener: (data: PixelDataState | Uint8Array) => void) {\n    this.#listeners.push(listener);\n  }\n\n  /**\n   * Handle pointer events (implements EventListener interface)\n   */\n  handleEvent(e: PointerEvent): void {\n    switch (e.type) {\n      case \"pointerdown\": {\n        this.#el.setPointerCapture(e.pointerId);\n        // Clear painted set for new drag\n        this.#painted.clear();\n        // Fall through to paint\n      }\n      // eslint-disable-next-line no-fallthrough\n      case \"pointermove\": {\n        // Convert canvas pixels to artboard pixels\n        const x = Math.floor(\n          (this.#artboard.w * e.offsetX) / this.#el.clientWidth\n        );\n        const y = Math.floor(\n          (this.#artboard.h * e.offsetY) / this.#el.clientHeight\n        );\n\n        // Update coordinate display\n        if (x >= 0 && x < this.#artboard.w && y >= 0 && y < this.#artboard.h) {\n          this.#onCoordChange?.(x, y);\n        }\n\n        if (e.type === \"pointermove\" && !this.#el.hasPointerCapture(e.pointerId)) {\n          // Just hovering - show cursor position\n          this.#drawCursorHighlight(x, y);\n          return;\n        }\n\n        this.#paint(x, y);\n        this.#prev = [x, y];\n        break;\n      }\n      case \"pointerup\": {\n        this.#el.releasePointerCapture(e.pointerId);\n        this.#prev = undefined;\n        this.#painted.clear();\n        // Clear cursor highlight\n        this.#clearOverlay();\n        break;\n      }\n      case \"pointerleave\": {\n        this.#onCoordChange?.(null, null);\n        this.#clearOverlay();\n        break;\n      }\n    }\n  }\n\n  /**\n   * Update cursor style based on tool mode\n   */\n  #updateCursor(): void {\n    this.#el.classList.remove(\"cursor-pencil\", \"cursor-eraser\");\n    this.#el.classList.add(\n      this.#toolMode === \"pencil\" ? \"cursor-pencil\" : \"cursor-eraser\"\n    );\n  }\n\n  /**\n   * Initialize the grid overlay\n   */\n  #initGrid(): void {\n    if (!this.#gridCanvas || !this.#gridCtx) return;\n\n    // Set up high-DPI grid canvas\n    this.#gridCanvas.width = this.#gridCanvas.clientWidth * devicePixelRatio;\n    this.#gridCanvas.height = this.#gridCanvas.clientHeight * devicePixelRatio;\n    this.#gridCtx.scale(devicePixelRatio, devicePixelRatio);\n\n    this.#drawGrid();\n  }\n\n  /**\n   * Draw the grid lines\n   */\n  #drawGrid(): void {\n    if (!this.#gridCtx || !this.#gridCanvas) return;\n\n    const ctx = this.#gridCtx;\n    const width = this.#gridCanvas.clientWidth;\n    const height = this.#gridCanvas.clientHeight;\n    const cellW = width / this.#artboard.w;\n    const cellH = height / this.#artboard.h;\n\n    ctx.clearRect(0, 0, width, height);\n    ctx.strokeStyle = \"rgba(100, 100, 120, 0.3)\";\n    ctx.lineWidth = 0.5;\n\n    // Draw vertical lines\n    for (let x = 0; x <= this.#artboard.w; x++) {\n      ctx.beginPath();\n      ctx.moveTo(x * cellW, 0);\n      ctx.lineTo(x * cellW, height);\n      ctx.stroke();\n    }\n\n    // Draw horizontal lines\n    for (let y = 0; y <= this.#artboard.h; y++) {\n      ctx.beginPath();\n      ctx.moveTo(0, y * cellH);\n      ctx.lineTo(width, y * cellH);\n      ctx.stroke();\n    }\n  }\n\n  /**\n   * Update grid visibility\n   */\n  #updateGridVisibility(): void {\n    if (this.#gridCanvas) {\n      this.#gridCanvas.classList.toggle(\"visible\", this.#showGrid);\n    }\n  }\n\n  /**\n   * Draw cursor highlight on overlay\n   */\n  #drawCursorHighlight(x: number, y: number): void {\n    if (!this.#overlayCtx || !this.#overlayCanvas) return;\n\n    const ctx = this.#overlayCtx;\n    const width = this.#overlayCanvas.clientWidth;\n    const height = this.#overlayCanvas.clientHeight;\n    const cellW = width / this.#artboard.w;\n    const cellH = height / this.#artboard.h;\n\n    ctx.clearRect(0, 0, width, height);\n\n    // Bounds check\n    if (x < 0 || x >= this.#artboard.w || y < 0 || y >= this.#artboard.h) {\n      return;\n    }\n\n    // Draw highlight rectangle\n    ctx.strokeStyle = \"rgba(108, 92, 231, 0.8)\";\n    ctx.lineWidth = 2;\n    ctx.strokeRect(x * cellW + 1, y * cellH + 1, cellW - 2, cellH - 2);\n  }\n\n  /**\n   * Clear the overlay canvas\n   */\n  #clearOverlay(): void {\n    if (this.#overlayCtx && this.#overlayCanvas) {\n      this.#overlayCtx.clearRect(\n        0,\n        0,\n        this.#overlayCanvas.clientWidth,\n        this.#overlayCanvas.clientHeight\n      );\n    }\n  }\n\n  /**\n   * Paint a pixel and draw a line from previous position\n   */\n  #paint(x: number, y: number): void {\n    // Bounds check\n    if (x < 0 || this.#artboard.w <= x) return;\n    if (y < 0 || this.#artboard.h <= y) return;\n\n    // Get the effective color (white for eraser)\n    const effectiveColor: RGB =\n      this.#toolMode === \"eraser\" ? [255, 255, 255] : this.#color;\n\n    // Paint with brush size\n    this.#paintWithBrush(x, y, effectiveColor);\n\n    // Draw line from previous position using DDA algorithm\n    if (this.#prev) {\n      const [px, py] = this.#prev;\n      this.#drawLine(px, py, x, y, effectiveColor);\n    }\n\n    this.#draw();\n    this.#notify();\n    this.#updateFillRate();\n  }\n\n  /**\n   * Paint with brush size consideration\n   */\n  #paintWithBrush(x: number, y: number, color: RGB): void {\n    const size = this.#brushSize;\n    const halfSize = Math.floor(size / 2);\n\n    for (let dy = 0; dy < size; dy++) {\n      for (let dx = 0; dx < size; dx++) {\n        const px = x - halfSize + dx;\n        const py = y - halfSize + dy;\n\n        // Bounds check\n        if (px < 0 || this.#artboard.w <= px) continue;\n        if (py < 0 || this.#artboard.h <= py) continue;\n\n        // Timestamp optimization: skip if already painted in this drag\n        const key = PixelData.key(px, py);\n        if (this.#painted.has(key)) continue;\n        this.#painted.add(key);\n\n        this.#data.set(px, py, color);\n      }\n    }\n  }\n\n  /**\n   * Draw a line between two points using DDA algorithm\n   */\n  #drawLine(x0: number, y0: number, x1: number, y1: number, color: RGB): void {\n    const dx = x1 - x0;\n    const dy = y1 - y0;\n    const steps = Math.max(Math.abs(dx), Math.abs(dy));\n\n    if (steps === 0) return;\n\n    const xInc = dx / steps;\n    const yInc = dy / steps;\n\n    let x = x0;\n    let y = y0;\n\n    for (let i = 0; i < steps; i++) {\n      x += xInc;\n      y += yInc;\n      const ix = Math.round(x);\n      const iy = Math.round(y);\n\n      this.#paintWithBrush(ix, iy, color);\n    }\n  }\n\n  /**\n   * Draw all pixels to canvas\n   */\n  async #draw(): Promise<void> {\n    const chans = 4; // RGBA\n    const buffer = new Uint8ClampedArray(\n      this.#artboard.w * this.#artboard.h * chans\n    );\n    const rowsize = this.#artboard.w * chans;\n\n    for (let row = 0; row < this.#artboard.h; row++) {\n      const offsetY = row * rowsize;\n      for (let col = 0; col < this.#artboard.w; col++) {\n        const offsetX = col * chans;\n        const offset = offsetY + offsetX;\n\n        const [r, g, b] = this.#data.get(col, row);\n        buffer[offset] = r;\n        buffer[offset + 1] = g;\n        buffer[offset + 2] = b;\n        buffer[offset + 3] = 255; // Alpha\n      }\n    }\n\n    const data = new ImageData(buffer, this.#artboard.w, this.#artboard.h);\n    const bitmap = await createImageBitmap(data);\n    this.#ctx.drawImage(\n      bitmap,\n      0,\n      0,\n      this.#el.clientWidth,\n      this.#el.clientHeight\n    );\n  }\n\n  /**\n   * Notify listeners of state change\n   */\n  #notify(): void {\n    const state = this.#data.state;\n\n    if (this.#compressionMode === \"binary\" && this.#encoder) {\n      this.#onCompressionStatus?.(\"Compressing...\");\n      const encoded = this.#encoder.encode(state);\n      this.#onCompressionStatus?.(\"Ready\");\n      for (const listener of this.#listeners) {\n        listener(encoded);\n      }\n    } else {\n      for (const listener of this.#listeners) {\n        listener(state);\n      }\n    }\n  }\n\n  /**\n   * Calculate and report fill rate\n   */\n  #updateFillRate(): void {\n    if (!this.#onFillRateChange) return;\n\n    const state = this.#data.state;\n    const totalPixels = this.#artboard.w * this.#artboard.h;\n    const filledPixels = Object.keys(state).length;\n    const rate = (filledPixels / totalPixels) * 100;\n\n    this.#onFillRateChange(rate);\n  }\n\n  /**\n   * Receive and merge remote state\n   */\n  receive(data: PixelDataState | Uint8Array): void {\n    if (this.#compressionMode === \"binary\" && this.#decoder && data instanceof Uint8Array) {\n      const { state } = this.#decoder.decode(data);\n      this.#data.merge(state);\n    } else if (data instanceof Uint8Array) {\n      throw new Error(\"Received binary data but binary mode is not enabled\");\n    } else {\n      this.#data.merge(data);\n    }\n    this.#draw();\n    this.#updateFillRate();\n  }\n\n  /**\n   * Get the current state\n   */\n  get state(): PixelDataState {\n    return this.#data.state;\n  }\n\n  /**\n   * Get the current artboard size\n   */\n  get artboard(): ArtboardSize {\n    return { ...this.#artboard };\n  }\n\n  /**\n   * Clear the canvas (set all pixels to white)\n   */\n  clear(): void {\n    // Create a new empty state\n    const state = this.#data.state;\n    for (const key in state) {\n      delete state[key];\n    }\n    this.#draw();\n    this.#updateFillRate();\n    this.#notify();\n  }\n}"}],"isError":false,"timestamp":1772597996474}}
{"type":"message","id":"50913f85","parentId":"b0fc0151","timestamp":"2026-03-04T04:20:05.676Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"I can see the file structure. The `clear()` method is at the end of the class. I need to add the `destroy()` method after it. The constructor adds event listeners for:\n- pointerdown\n- pointermove\n- pointerup\n- pointerleave\n\nSo the destroy method needs to remove all these listeners and clear the #listeners array.\n\nLet me add the destroy() method after the clear() method.","thinkingSignature":"reasoning_content"},{"type":"text","text":"Now I'll add the `destroy()` method after the `clear()` method:"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"tool-7dcb3f1dbbf74d82bd91e54694a9281c","name":"edit","arguments":{"file_path":"/home/one/projects/PixelArtEditor/src/editor/PixelEditor.ts","oldText":"/**\n   * Clear the canvas (set all pixels to white)\n   */\n  clear(): void {\n    // Create a new empty state\n    const state = this.#data.state;\n    for (const key in state) {\n      delete state[key];\n    }\n    this.#draw();\n    this.#updateFillRate();\n    this.#notify();\n  }\n}","newText":"/**\n   * Clear the canvas (set all pixels to white)\n   */\n  clear(): void {\n    // Create a new empty state\n    const state = this.#data.state;\n    for (const key in state) {\n      delete state[key];\n    }\n    this.#draw();\n    this.#updateFillRate();\n    this.#notify();\n  }\n\n  /**\n   * Clean up event listeners and resources\n   * Call this when the editor is no longer needed\n   */\n  destroy(): void {\n    this.#el.removeEventListener(\"pointerdown\", this);\n    this.#el.removeEventListener(\"pointermove\", this);\n    this.#el.removeEventListener(\"pointerup\", this);\n    this.#el.removeEventListener(\"pointerleave\", this);\n    this.#listeners = [];\n  }\n}"}}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"bailian","model":"glm-5","usage":{"input":4027,"output":453,"cacheRead":12262,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":1674