{"type":"message","id":"0c234d38","parentId":"7224296a","timestamp":"2026-03-04T04:20:31.369Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Now I'll write the development report to the shared directory.","thinkingSignature":"reasoning_content"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"tool-839c31c3cc8048f6adbbc5fe87c44eed","name":"write","arguments":{"file_path":"/home/one/.openclaw-reports/code-agent/2025-03-04-destroy-method.md","content":"# Development Report\n\n**Date:** 2025-03-04\n**Task:** Add destroy() method to PixelEditor\n**Agent:** code-agent\n\n## Workspace\n`/home/one/projects/PixelArtEditor`\n\n## Files Changed\n| File | Description |\n|------|-------------|\n| `src/editor/PixelEditor.ts` | Added destroy() method for cleanup |\n\n## Implementation Summary\n- Added `destroy()` method to PixelEditor class\n- Method removes all four event listeners: pointerdown, pointermove, pointerup, pointerleave\n- Clears the listeners array to prevent any future callbacks\n- Method placed after `clear()` method as requested\n\n## Code Notes\nThe `destroy()` method uses the `handleEvent` pattern - the class itself implements `EventListener`, so `this` is passed as both the listener reference and removed via `removeEventListener`.\n\n```typescript\ndestroy(): void {\n  this.#el.removeEventListener(\"pointerdown\", this);\n  this.#el.removeEventListener(\"pointermove\", this);\n  this.#el.removeEventListener(\"pointerup\", this);\n  this.#el.removeEventListener(\"pointerleave\", this);\n  this.#listeners = [];\n}\n```\n\n## Verification\n- ✅ TypeScript compilation: `npx tsc --noEmit` - passed (no errors)\n- ✅ Tests: `npm test` - 42 tests passed, 4 suites\n\n## Status\n✅ Ready for use"}}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"bailian","model":"glm-5","usage":{"input":39,"output":351,"cacheRead":16774,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":17164,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1772598022442}}
